{"name":"Urban Oasis","hex":"#374f54","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"urban","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, characteristic of, or happening or located in, a city or town; of, pertaining to, or characteristic of life in such a place, especially when contrasted with the countryside.","Living in a city or town."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urban"},{"term":"oasis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spring of fresh water, surrounded by a fertile region of vegetation, in a desert.","A quiet, peaceful place or situation separated from surrounding noise or bustle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oasis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Urban oasis","blocks":[{"text":"An urban oasis is a public open space, park, or plaza which is located in between buildings or formed by surrounding buildings in an urban setting. It can exist in any kind of culture. There are various sizes of urban oases. Central Park, Frederick Law Olmsted's park in New York City, can be considered as a very large urban oasis. The Los Angeles Central Library’s plaza can be considered to be a small scaled oasis."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_oasis"},{"title":"Oasis","blocks":[{"text":"An oasis is a fertile area of a desert or semi-desert environment that sustains plant life and provides habitat for animals. Surface water may be present, or water may only be accessible from wells or underground channels created by humans. In geography, an oasis may be a current or past rest stop on a transportation route, or less-than-verdant location that nonetheless provides access to underground water through deep wells created and maintained by humans. Although they depend on a natural condition, such as the presence of water that may be stored in reservoirs and used for irrigation, most oases, as we know them, are artificial."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/ISS-64_Jubba_with_Nefud_Desert%2C_Saudi_Arabia.jpg/330px-ISS-64_Jubba_with_Nefud_Desert%2C_Saudi_Arabia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oasis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Hastings_Creek.jpg/500px-Hastings_Creek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Hastings_Creek.jpg/500px-Hastings_Creek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hastings Creek, Vancouver[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHastings_Creek.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Indira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_%2811%29.jpg/500px-Indira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Indira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_%2811%29.jpg/1280px-Indira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Indira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_%2811%29.jpg/500px-Indira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indira Park, Hyderabad, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndira_Park_Hyderabad-Dr_Murali_Mohan_Gurram_(11).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg/500px-Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg/500px-Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.